{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* Echoed damage is calculated by taking the pre-mitigation damage against the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}, applying ''Test of Spirit's'' damage modifier, and then capping it to the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} {{as|'''current''' health}}. This damage will then be affected by damage modifiers (resistances and other effects) of the {{as|Vessel|buzzword3}}.
** This order of operations allows ''Test of Spirit'' to deal more or less percentage of the {{as|Vessel's|buzzword3}} {{as|health}} than would be expected:
**# Because the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} modifiers can be different from the {{as|Vessel's|buzzword3}}, allowing the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} to have higher or lower [[health|effective health]], respectively increasing or decreasing the maximum pre-mitigated damage from killing it.
**# Because, while it would be expected to block excess pre-mitigated damage over what kills the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}, since the cap does not consider the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} damage modifier, it may cause it to block damage before the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} is killed [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y2ASLYcuTXE], or in corner cases not block excess damage even if it is killed. On the other hand, ''Test of Spirit's'' damage modifier is unexpectedly applied before the cap instead of after, with the same effect of potentially causing the cap to not block excess damage even if the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} is killed, or in corner cases block damage before it is killed.
**#* The addition of the two, causes an increasing difference of expected damage when the pre-mitigated damage is between <code>Spirit current health{{divided by}}Spiritmod</code> and <code>Spirit current health{{divided by}}Emod</code>. {{bug|2}}|affectedEffects=Illaoi E|estimatedPatchOrigin=V5.23|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1773991211|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Illaoi/Test of Spirit
}}
** '''Illaoi''' needs {{as|{{ap|(100-(25 to 45))/8*100}} '''total''' AD}} to reach 100% echoed damage. As per above, the damage is still dependent on the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} and {{as|Vessel's|buzzword3}} damage modifiers and may not always be able to deal 100% of the target's '''current''' health as total echoed damage.
* Transferred damage will apply on-damage effects, such as damage amplifiers (e.g {{ri|Last Stand}}), {{ii|Black Cleaver}}, {{ii|Morellonomicon}}, {{ii|Executioner's Calling}}, {{ii|Elixir of Sorcery}}, {{ri|Sudden Impact}}, {{ii|Shadowflame}}, {{ii|The Collector}}, {{ri|First Strike}}, {{bi|Aspect of the Dragon}} burn damage, and {{ai|The Darkin Scythe A|Shadow Assassin|The Darkin Scythe}}.
** Echoed damage always counts as single target for the purpose of {{tip|Omnivamp}}.
** Echoed damage always counts as {{tip|proc damage}} and thus will not doubly apply on-hit or on-spell effects versus the target (e.g. {{ii|Liandry's Torment}}). These effects are only applied versus the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}.
** Some effects like {{ri|Sudden Impact}} are consumed by the target first, before the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}. Other effects like {{ii|Hextech Alternator}} are consumed by the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} first, before the target.
** Attacking the {{as|Vessel|buzzword3}} and its {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} simultaneously will only apply one stack of {{ii|Black Cleaver}} to the {{as|Vessel|buzzword3}}.<!--
